  <p>We are here to help. Questions, complaints, and disagreement are welcome. Threats, harassment, discriminatory language, sexual content directed at others, and abusive or obscene language are not acceptable. These expectations apply to visitors and support team members alike.</p>
  <p>Live Chat automatically replaces recognized swear words with **** and displays a reminder. The filter may not recognize every variation; support members also review conversations.</p>
  <h2>When a conversation is flagged</h2>
  <p>A support member may flag a conversation for Community Standards and explain the expectations. If communication remains abusive or unproductive, the team may end the chat. You can still submit a support ticket to ask for follow-up or escalation of your concerns.</p>
  <h2>Choose the right support channel</h2>
  <p>Live Chat is for quick questions and begins when a support member sends you a message. Availability can change. For detailed concerns, unresolved frustrations, or information that needs review by the full support team, submit a ticket using the inquiry button in chat or the website contact page.</p>
  <p>You may submit contact information and an inquiry at any time, including while waiting for a reply, and return to your chat afterward. Closing the chat on the staff side preserves the conversation so another support member can return.</p>
